Pro:
+Maybe the music; it's decent at least for this kind of game.
+Relatively easy unlock of achivements;
Cons:
- Buggy, unoptimized;
- Locked in full screen & no option to turn down the volume if you would prefer so;
- There's 2 game modes but they're the same, only in one you waste more time proceeding (and I assume you play the levels in an order), while in the other you get to select the level;
- You get weapons and power ups and don't even know what they do;
- Your hit boxes are too big and unfair, enemies kill you from not even touching you;
- The shield you get is useless, makes no difference whatsoever (well it spares you from death once but the hitboxes issue mentioned above makes you just wanna die without shield, anyway).
As it stands, it's not worth 1 $ / eur. as of now (yea I know, right ?), not only because of the cons. it comes with, but because for the same price you get a -way- better indie game experience, if you look enough in the Store. Or possibly add a bit more money and get a real game of the kind *cough*
*cough* via trading or from a sale.

A gem of a game, not what I expected at all. It has innovative gameplay, an original storyline, and damn detailed side quest gameplay (also if you have a decent rig to play this on...well the graphics and effects are top shelf). In the end if you like crime solving games with a splash of supernatural... this game is well worth it. I highly recomend it indeed.
-Side Note (metascore);
-For the first time I really question the metascore, critics reviewing this baffle me... the users reviews are a bit more on par and fairer in their assessment... I guess in the end just watch some let's plays and see what your close friends think of it and thats that.

